.build/
.swiftpm/
# Package.resolved is COMMITTED, not ignored, since the CLI took its first dependency.
# `from: "0.12.1"` has to be a range — both consumers already pin swift-sdk `exact: "0.12.1"`
# and two exact requirements on one package must agree forever — but a range with no lockfile
# means this repo's own CI resolves the newest 0.x on every run, and pre-1.0 SemVer promises
# nothing. A breaking 0.13.0 would land here unannounced while both consumers, pinned exactly,
# saw nothing. Committing it pins OUR builds only: SwiftPM reads the ROOT package's lockfile
# and ignores a dependency's, so no consumer is constrained by this file.
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace
DerivedData/
.DS_Store
dist/
.env
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
.cursor/
